{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526303-v20-developing-backgrounds-in-game","id":1526303,"title":"[V20] Developing backgrounds in game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-03T17:38:11-08:00","id":1526303,"title":"[V20] Developing backgrounds in game","content":"Started a game lacking in contacts yet you're now the one with everybody on speed dial? Had no friends but can now call a werewolf pack (Somehow) to help you take down the prince? Had to go weeks without feeding yet now have an entire town willing to lend you an artery? <br /> <br /> Let us know how you did it! For reasons I won't make EXTREMELY obvious, be as specific as possible! ... please! <br /> <br /> Let's also play a little game! Imagine you're a Ventrue who was originally planned to be a sophisticated/Charismatic monster who gained a sick pleasure in destroying the lives of young women with bright futures but even after deciding that isn't the type of vampire you play basically kept the feeding restriction. How would you go about forming a Herd of that restriction? Once again, obviously just a fun game within this thread! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In all seriousness, I'm hoping for some advice as my Ventrue has survived but not thrived for quite some time and I'm hoping to build up his backgrounds. He was my first ever creation outside of the videogame and I didn't truly respect my ST's suggestions and I'm feeling it having no real control over any situation and I'm trying to build up a bit. I have decent social skills (Sadly, in game only) with a big advantage in leadership type skills, I have a self imposed roleplay restriction with dominate so only have presence (3 for now but my next step is to increase). What did you all do to build up from zero and what things do you think a Ventrue living in Beverly Hills should probably focus on first? I do have 5 points in resources which is personal wealth for my character more than a network of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27150-minnzy","name":"Minnzy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-03T20:13:12-08:00","id":1526310,"title":"","content":"Backgrounds are one of those things that can be like pulling teeth to get or you can rack up multiple dots per play session, it really depends on the game and the ST.<br /> <br /> To make Backgrounds a primary focus for a character, I tend to go with a &quot;Boon Generator&quot; build. Any Clan with Dominate as a discipline makes this much easier, I think the easiest is a Tremere. With one dot in Auspex and one in Dominate you go down to your local gambling places and clean up vs. players rather than the house. The Auspex lets you read tells more easily or simply read the card reflections in the other players eyes. Dominate in this case allows you to hide one word poker commands inside banter at the table. This more or less gets you Resources 3 to 4 with little in the way of traceable footprint. As such you can start using the money to finance useful businesses or make upgrades to improve your survivability. Once that is done you can use that extra money to do favors for other kindred, for a favor in return of course.<br /> <br /> Once Dominate gets to level 3, offer your services to neonates to assist with cleanups regarding masquerade infractions. This way the Prince or the Sheriff don't get cranky about it and you earn some favors. This is where investing in a Crime Scene Clean Up service actually becomes very useful. The neonate calls you, agree upon the payment/favor owed, then you send your employees to clean up the site while you do memory cleaning. Just doing this sort of thing over time will build Allies, Contacts, Influence, Resources, and Status scores.<br /> <br /> With enough Resources, you then can in turn find the best Retainers available in the area. Furthermore, if you start cracking into the Resources 4 to 5 range then you can start investing/owning businesses which give secondary benefits. Owning a minor construction business means that you can have work crews on speed dial if you want to have project done faster than normally possible or just done during nighttime. If you take over a medical clinic, you can offer off the book's medical services for things like gunshots or supernatural wounds on other kindred's mortal retainers. Get your fingers into a mortuary business and you can sell all kinds of parts to magically inclined kindred or other critters with exotic shopping lists.<br /> <br /> In essence you build Resources until the Background is self-sustaining, then gain businesses that give you all sorts of perks. You then share those perks with the kindred community for a fair price. This means you are too helpful to kill but you also know who is up to what, which means you can trade in information or just make sure your interests are out of collateral damage range from another kindreds plans. Also, anyone who comes after you will have to contend not only with your personal power, but also every other kindred who finds you useful to have around. Power and influence begets more contacts and resources which in turn leads to more power &amp; influence.<br /> <br /> Herd is a Background which doesn't have a generic answer to how to build because it depends on the character. A Nosferatu Herd is just some homeless tunnel dwellers that trade blood for the food or medicine the nosferatu can steal for them. If your character owns a hospital, then the herd is essentially the blood bank or the coma patients. Conversely a vampire with Presence or Dominate can easily acquire babies and raise them to be perfect servants and blood donors. I have had players who did the whole hidden society thing where the children raised were taught dead languages so that even if they did want to turn against their vampire liege, they couldn't communicate anything to the wider world.<br /> <br /> Once you get this established then you just start to diversify your holdings and power base so that no one attack or calamity can break you. After that it is just a question of time, which as an immortal, a vampire has in ample supply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T19:07:17-08:00","id":1526386,"title":"","content":"A lot of my games, they started out as mortals first, so they had to build their backgrounds. Backgrounds are tools for the ST and the players if they need something, like herd or resources, but it isn't important to the story to explain it. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526303-v20-developing-backgrounds-in-game?p=1526310#post1526310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Backgrounds are one of those things that can be like pulling teeth to get or you can rack up multiple dots per play session, it really depends on the game and the ST.<br /> . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true; the players, have to actually think about it and suggested; most ST's are too busy. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}